# Golden tests are the oracle

`testdata/golden/` holds outputs produced by the pinned TASSEL 5 release (see
ADR-0009 and `testdata/golden/MANIFEST`). A ported analysis is correct when it
matches them.

- Never edit, regenerate, or delete files in `testdata/golden/` unless the issue
  explicitly asks for it. If a golden test fails, fix the port or stop and
  report. Do not "update the expectation".
- Never loosen a tolerance to make a test pass. Tolerances are set per analysis
  in the golden manifest; changing one needs an ADR or the maintainer's ok.
- Put tests in `commonTest` so they run on every target. Use a
  platform-specific test source set only for platform code.

# Comparison conventions

- Doubles: absolute tolerance from the manifest (kinship uses `8e-6`, matching
  TASSEL 5's `CenteredIBSTest`).
- PCA: compare eigenvalues directly; compare each eigenvector up to sign
  (normalize so the largest-magnitude entry is positive, then compare).
- Tables: compare headers, row order, and column order exactly, then values.
- Text output: compare after normalizing line endings only.

```kotlin
// BAD
assertEquals(expected, actual, 1e-3) // loosened until green

// GOOD
assertMatrixEquals(golden.kinship, actual, tolerance = manifest.tolerance("kinship"))
```

# Test data access

Load files through the shared `TestData` helper so the same test runs on the
JVM, Node (wasmJs), and Native. Do not use `java.io.File` or classpath
resources in `commonTest`.
